#. module: nudge_connect
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:nudge_connect.field_nudge_connector__cache_ttl
msgid ""
"A Read tool's answer is kept this long for the same person, company and "
"arguments, so that asking again in a conversation does not reach the server."
" 0 is off (the default); 60 is a good start; at most 3600. Writes are never "
"kept, and what is kept is still data, never an instruction."
msgstr ""

#. module: nudge_connect
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:nudge_connect.res_config_settings_view_form_connect
msgid ""
"A call to a connector costs no tokens but counts as one call. A person who "
"reached the limit is told, and nothing is sent. A kept answer is not a call."
" 0 is no limit."
msgstr ""

#. module: nudge_connect
#: model_terms:ir.actions.act_window,help:nudge_connect.nudge_connector_action
msgid ""
"A connector is an outside system that speaks MCP: a sister company's Odoo, a calendar, a chat,\n"
"                a document store. Add its address, read its tools, and allow the ones Nudge may use: reads run\n"
"                for the person, writes wait for their yes."
msgstr ""

#. module: nudge_connect
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:nudge_connect.field_nudge_connector__preset
msgid ""
"A ready-made starting point: it fills the address, the kind of credential "
"and the tools that come in as Read. It does not promise the server exists: "
"the tools are read from the server, and every one comes in Not Allowed "
"except those the preset marks Read."
msgstr ""

#. module: nudge_connect
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:nudge_connect.field_nudge_connector__key
msgid ""
"A short name of small letters, digits and _: the tools are called "
"cx_<key>__<tool>."
msgstr ""

#. module: nudge_connect
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:nudge_connect.nudge_connector_view_form
msgid ""
"A tool comes in Not Allowed. Open it, read what it says and what it takes, and\n"
"                                allow it as Read (runs at once for the person) or Write (the person sees exactly\n"
"                                what is sent and says yes first). A tool whose description changes on the server\n"
"                                is not allowed any more until it is allowed again."
msgstr ""

